<template><article class="method-page"><h1>The numbers.<br><span class="accent">And their limits.</span></h1><p class="lead">BuildValue helps you understand what an item costs and what its base stats buy. It does not rank builds by win rate or simulate combat.</p><section><h2>One patch, one set of references.</h2><p>Items and artwork come from Riot's public <a href="https://developer.riotgames.com/docs/lol#data-dragon">Data Dragon</a>. The app checks its versions feed on startup. If that request fails, the bundled snapshot keeps the explorer usable.</p><div class="method-equation">Stat efficiency = priced stat value ÷ total cost × 100</div><p>Currently showing patch <strong>{{ dataset.version }}</strong> from {{ source }}. Data Dragon releases can lag regional game patches.</p><p>Only purchasable Summoner's Rift items are shown. Champion-specific and hidden items are excluded using the dataset's flags, not a list of retired names.</p></section><section><h2>What gets priced?</h2><p>For each supported stat, we divide a basic item's total cost by its stat amount in the same patch. Then we apply that reference rate to the selected item's stats.</p><div class="method-table"><table><thead><tr><th>Stat</th><th>Reference item</th><th>Reference cost</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr v-for="(definition, key) in statDefinitions" :key="key"><td>{{ definition.label }}</td><td>{{ dataset.data[definition.reference]?.name }}</td><td>{{ number(dataset.data[definition.reference]?.gold.total || 0) }} G</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Passives, actives, ability haste, penetration, regeneration, lifesteal, percentage movement speed, and other unsupported stats are not assigned a gold value. Descriptions remain visible so you can assess those effects yourself. Build totals simply add supported stats; they do not simulate stacking rules or item restrictions.</p><p>Low or zero efficiency can reflect missing priced stats, not a bad item. A high number does not mean an item is right for your champion.</p></section><section><h2>A working application of Forza UI.</h2><p>The interface uses the published Forza UI package for inputs, selectors, buttons, dialogs, drawers, lists, and pagination. BuildValue owns the game data and calculations. <a href="https://forzaui.chrisdalbano.com/guide/buildvalue">See the integration guide ↗</a></p><p>Created by <a href="https://chrisdalbano.com">Chrisdalbano</a> with AI assistance across research, code, design iteration, and documentation. Source and checks are public on <a href="https://github.com/Chrisdalbano/valuebuild-web">GitHub</a>. This project is independent and not endorsed by Riot Games.</p></section></article></template>
